WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:03.700
Narrator: Hillsborough, England, 1989.

2
00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:08.400
Narrator: Too few turnstiles meant a huge crowd built up outside.

3
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.740
Narrator: An exit gate was opened to relieve the pressure.

4
00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:22.300
Narrator: Fans walked straight down a tunnel into central pens that were already full - while the side pens had space.

5
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.920
Narrator: No one closed the tunnel or directed fans to the side pens.

6
00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:35.930
Narrator: The central pens became so packed that people were crushed against the fences and a barrier gave way.

7
00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:40.240
Narrator: Ninety-seven people died.

8
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.960
Narrator: The fans were not to blame.

9
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.090
Narrator: The lessons: watch each area, not the total.

10
00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.520
Narrator: Act on signs of distress early.

11
00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:55.320
Narrator: Direct people to where there is space.

12
00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.350
Narrator: Report areas where space is becoming limited.

